{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/kemenyConstant(weight:)-8j44l"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kemenyConstant","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"},{"kind":"text","text":"? "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sz","text":"BinaryInteger"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vol · (Σᵢ πᵢ (L_g⁻¹)ᵢᵢ − πᵀ L_g⁻¹ π), π the stationary distribution, which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(1\/2vol) Σᵢⱼ dᵢ dⱼ R(i, j) (commute times are vol · R), with L_g the Laplacian grounded at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the vertex of largest degree and eliminated as for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"numberOfSpanningTrees"},{"type":"text","text":". Every term is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sum of positive ones and the difference loses at most a factor n, so the result keeps its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"relative accuracy under any weight spread. O(n³) time, n² "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":"s."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"weight","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the weight of the edge at each position, read once per position; a weight of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"0 is no edge."}]},{"type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every weight is finite and nonnegative."}]}],"style":"note","name":"Precondition"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"The Kemeny constant: the expected number of steps of the random walk (edge weights as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"transition rates, a loop taken with probability 2w\/d(v)) from a vertex to a target drawn","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from the stationary distribution, which does not depend on the start; Σ_{i≥2} 1\/μᵢ over the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"normalized Laplacian spectrum. nil when the graph is not connected, 0 for zero or one vertex.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph\/kemenyconstant(weight:)-8j44l"]}],"metadata":{"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","roleHeading":"Instance Method","symbolKind":"method","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SpectralGraphTheory\/ElectricalNetworks.swift#L286","fileName":"ElectricalNetworks.swift"},"modules":[